    "bugs": {
      "17824": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
            "time": "2020-06-07T14:42:49Z",
            "id": 95921,
            "is_private": false,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "creation_time": "2020-06-07T14:42:49Z",
            "text": "R 4.0.0 adds support for more helpful stopifnot() usage like:\n\n> x = 20\n> stopifnot('the input is too large' = x < 10)\n\nHowever, tools::update_pkg_po() does not detect these messages as translatable string literals.\n\nA minimal package:\n\n> cd /tmp\n> mkdir testPkg && cd testPkg\n> echo 'Package: testPkg' > DESCRIPTION\n> echo 'Version: 0.0.1' >> DESCRIPTION\n> mkdir R\n> echo \"foo = function(x) stopifnot('the input is too large' = x < 10)\" >\n> R/test.R\n> echo 'export(foo)' > NAMESPACE\n\nRunning update_pkg_po:\n\n> Rscript -e \"tools::update_pkg_po('.')\"\n\nbuilds the po directory and .pot file:\n\n> cat po/R-testPkg.pot\n> # msgid \"\"\n> # msgstr \"\"\n> # \"Project-Id-Version: testPkg 0.0.1\\n\"\n> # \"POT-Creation-Date: 2020-06-07 22:33\\n\"\n> # \"PO-Revision-Date: YEAR-MO-DA HO:MI+ZONE\\n\"\n> # \"Last-Translator: FULL NAME <EMAIL@ADDRESS>\\n\"\n> # \"Language-Team: LANGUAGE <LL@li.org>\\n\"\n> # \"MIME-Version: 1.0\\n\"\n> # \"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=CHARSET\\n\"\n> # \"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\\n\"\n\nNothing about \"the input is too large\"",
            "bug_id": 17824,
            "is_markdown": false,
            "count": 0
          },
          {
            "is_markdown": false,
            "count": 1,
            "bug_id": 17824,
            "text": "Created attachment 2630\nstopifnot gains domain argument, and tools::xgettext reads these messages\n\nupdate_pkg_po('.') in the patch captures the message from the above example.\n\n 1. Added domain= argument to stopifnot, which only applies to the new 4.0.0 use case\n 2. Adjusted the logic in tools::xgettext to look for stopifnot() calls (in addition to the existing stop(), warning(), ... calls). stopifnot() is slightly different in that it's the argument names, not the values, that we want to capture.\n\nTested on the sample package above & with make check-devel.",
            "creation_time": "2020-06-07T16:13:17Z",
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "is_private": false,
